# tools/ales_stereo_schmitt_witness.rish — stereo_schmitt: the Schmitt trigger carried into stereo with ONE SHARED BAND and TWO INDEPENDENT RAILS, the first state-carrying member of the comparator class lifted to stereo (ALES144).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES144.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-044135_fill-ales144-lotus-stereo-schmitt.md
# Stands on: lotus/schmitt.rye (ALES92 — the mono Schmitt trigger run once per channel, its from-silence schmitt, its carried SchmittTrigger, its precheck band-and-span law, and its SchmittError, all reused whole),
# lotus/stereo_infinite_clip.rye (ALES143 — the memoryless comparator whose odd antisymmetry this state-carrying member honestly parts from), lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip, two mono Clips left/right, and its
# balance invariant), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, its buf/len/samples, sample_min/max). A Lotus master is a StereoClip whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length. This rung carries
# ALES92's hysteresis into stereo — a rise past t_high flipping each channel's rail high, a fall past t_low flipping it low, a sample between holding, the band a dead zone the noise cannot rattle — running the proven mono
# schmitt on each channel with the same band, one dead zone landing on both speakers together. Where the just-closed stereo dead-zone family is memoryless, this carries one bit per channel: each channel remembers its own
# rail from the shared low-rail convention, so the two rails advance independently — an identical-channel master staying identical, an out-of-phase master NOT held out of phase (the honest parting from the memoryless odd
# family), and a two-piece StereoSchmitt run equalling the whole run once byte for byte on both channels (no seam flip), ALES92's carried-state crux carried into stereo.
#
# lotus/stereo_schmitt.rye validates the shared band and length once against ALES92's own precheck before either channel is mutated (BadThreshold on a band that is not two ordered thresholds inside the rails, BadRange on a
# span outside the samples), then triggers both channels through ALES92's schmitt; SchmittError reused whole. The crux is four laws. THE STEREO SCHMITT LAW: each channel equals ALES92's mono schmitt with the same band byte
# for byte. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after, both holding their starting length. THE INDEPENDENT-RAIL LAW: an identical master staying identical, an out-of-phase master not held out of phase, the two
# rails independent, the zero-width band the plain comparator on both. THE CARRIED-STATE / ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: a two-piece run equals the whole once byte for byte on both, a refusal leaves both channels and both
# rails untouched and balanced, count zero the identity.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_schmitt_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-schmitt: Language EN — stereo_schmitt triggers a span in both channels of a stereo master with the same band, flipping each channel's rail high on a rise past t_high, low on a fall past t_low, and holding between, so one dead zone lands on both speakers together. A Lotus master is two Clips heard together, one per speaker, whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length so the two channels stay aligned in time. This rung carries the first state-carrying member of the comparator class into stereo on ALES92's Schmitt trigger, running the proven mono schmitt on each channel with the same band, validated once against the shared band and length before either channel is mutated so a refusal never triggers one channel, or advances one rail, and leaves the other whole."
say "ales-stereo-schmitt: Style Radiant — the just-closed stereo dead-zone family (hard center clip, soft center clip, infinite clip) is memoryless: it judges each sample on its own. This rung is that class's state-carrying sibling, carrying one bit per channel, which rail am I on, so a signal riding near the level triggers on the event rather than chattering on the noise, the band between the two thresholds a dead zone the noise cannot rattle. It offers ALES92's two forms mirrored: stereo_schmitt runs each channel from silence on the low rail, and StereoSchmitt holds each channel's own trigger so a keeper carries the two rails beside the master. The honest signature of a state-carrying member in stereo is that each channel remembers its own rail, both opened from the same low-rail convention, so the two rails advance independently. An identical-channel master stays identical, the two rails tracking together, a mono-in-stereo signal never splitting. Yet an out-of-phase master, right the exact negation of left, does not in general come back out of phase, and this is where the state-carrying member honestly parts from the memoryless family: the from-silence convention opens both channels on the low rail, so the map is not odd about the band, and the antisymmetry the three clips held is a property of a memoryless odd map rather than of a comparator that remembers a shared low start. The crux is carried state across a seam: because each channel carries its own bit, a stereo span run in two pieces through StereoSchmitt, each channel's second piece continuing that channel's ending rail, equals the whole run once byte for byte on both channels, no spurious flip at the seam on either speaker, ALES92's own crux carried faithfully into stereo. The rule is stated positively: the trigger writes only the two rails plus or minus sample_max, both legal i16 so no saturate is owed, and never a length; it carries one band and names two faults. Refuse BadThreshold on a band that is not two ordered thresholds inside the rails, the zero-width band the legal plain comparator, and BadRange on a span outside the samples, each before either channel is touched, else trigger both channels through ALES92's schmitt. It reuses ALES92's SchmittError by name, ALES92's schmitt for the hysteresis, and ALES92's precheck for the band-and-span law, inventing no new fault and no new primitive. The crux stands out as four laws: the stereo schmitt law, the balance / length law, the independent-rail law (an identical master staying identical, an out-of-phase master not held out of phase, the two rails independent, the zero-width band the comparator on both), and the carried-state / atomicity / degenerate law (a two-piece run equalling the whole once byte for byte on both, any refusal leaving both channels and both rails untouched and balanced, count zero the identity)."
say "ales-stereo-schmitt: Lens TAME — two bounded i16 Clips (left, right) triggered in lockstep by one shared band, each carrying its own one bit of rail state; the balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit, the shared band and span are bound-checked once via ALES92's precheck before any write, and because those checks hold identically for both balanced channels each mono schmitt is pre-validated to succeed so no refusal can land between the two channel edits or advance a single rail; schmitt walks the span once per channel, comparing each sample in i32 so a threshold at the deep rail is representable, writing one of two signed rail constants per sample, never touching a byte past len so the length holds exactly; StereoSchmitt shares its band through a single init so left and right can never drift to different thresholds, threads each channel's carried rail through ALES92's SchmittTrigger, and resets both rails to low together; the stereo schmitt law is proven against ALES92's own schmitt run per channel, the independent-rail law proves an identical master stays identical while an out-of-phase master's channels both open on the shared low rail rather than negating and the two rails flip independently, the carried-state crux proves a two-piece StereoSchmitt run equals the whole once on both channels, and the atomicity cases leave both channels and both rails untouched with count zero the identity; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no time constant, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_schmitt"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_schmitt.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-schmitt: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_schmitt.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-schmitt: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-schmitt: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-schmitt' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-schmitt: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-schmitt line"
